      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Epimeteo pidió repartir los regalos, y Prometeo aceptó.",
          "en": "Epimetheus asked to hand out the gifts, and Prometheus agreed."
        },
        {
          "es": "Al león le dio garras y fuerza. A la gacela, patas veloces para escapar.",
          "en": "To the lion he gave claws and strength. To the gazelle, fast legs to escape."
        },
        {
          "es": "A las aves les dio alas, y al oso un abrigo grueso para el invierno.",
          "en": "To the birds he gave wings, and to the bear a thick coat for winter."
        },
        {
          "es": "Dio y dio sin pensar, hasta que no le quedó nada.",
          "en": "He gave and gave without thinking, until he had nothing left."
        },
        {
          "es": "Entonces vio que faltaba una criatura: el ser humano. Y ya no tenía ningún regalo para él.",
          "en": "Then he saw that one creature was missing: the human. And he had no gift left for it."
        }
